  "description": "Single-storey rear extension.",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed single storey rear extension, by reason of its 4m depth, height, siting directly along the shared boundary, and proximity to a glazed door serving the neighbouring dining room, would introduce a continuous built form alongside this opening. This door provides the main outlook and light to the dining room. The extension would therefore significantly restrict outlook and create an undue sense of enclosure to this habitable space.Thespace. The proposal would result in a material loss of residential amenity, contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD8 and DMD11 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
